cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the article that
  introduces the protocol.
title: "treatment-identity: verify that the treatment an experiment declares is the one its data loader delivers"
abstract: >-
  Eight CPU treatment-delivery gates probe the loader output declared by an
  experiment, and a separate geometry gate checks evaluation integrity.
  Release 1.9.0 extends the portability campaign from ten to sixteen loaders
  from fifteen projects (ProPainter, DiffuEraser, E2FGVI, VRT, LaMa and GFPGAN
  added) and corrects the defects those loaders exposed in the instrument:
  temporal indices erased by a fixed-size resize are reported as unreadable
  rather than as an inert sampler; the stored-input gate reads values in the
  declared numerical convention and requires both checkerboard anchors; an
  empty loader reaches the clip-length escalation; a declared count of zero
  target transforms is a declaration; adapter sizes no longer count
  docstrings; and subjects are isolated on the import path. It also carries
  the 2026-09-08 review corrections (declared conventions for separability,
  explicit exchangeability for paired inference, per-axis scale ratios).
